var SUITE={id:'suite',moduleId:'home',moduleTitle:'Document suite',title:'Standardized SE document suite (printable)',html:`<div class="eyebrow">Document templates · NASA / INCOSE aligned</div><h1 class="hero-title">Standardized SE document suite</h1><p class="lede">The complete portfolio toolkit in one place: seven core engineering documents (structured the way programs keep them — NASA NPR 7123 / ISO 15288 practice) plus all nineteen project artifact templates. Click a document or artifact card to open its fillable form; values persist in this browser and are shared with the teaching lessons. Use "<b>Open document · print/PDF</b>" or "<b>Open template · print/PDF</b>" inside any form to open a clean HTML page you can save as PDF (&ldquo;Print / Save as PDF&rdquo;). Content is placeholder-only, never real project data.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">7 documents</span><span class="tag">19 artifact templates</span><span class="tag">Autosaved locally</span><span class="tag">Print / save to PDF</span></div>
<div class="btnrow"><button class="btn" type="button" onclick="exportSuite('all')">Open entire suite as printable HTML</button></div>

<div class="section"><h2>Project artifact templates — click a card to open</h2><p class="mini">The nineteen fillable templates in the order you build them across the project. Each card carries a short description, its home module and a direct link to the teaching lesson. Click a card to open the fillable form, then use “Open template · print/PDF” to export it.</p>${artifactCardsHTML()}<div class="art-stage" id="artStage"></div></div>

<div class="section"><h2>Core documents — click a card to open a fillable form</h2><p class="mini">The seven core engineering documents, structured the way programs keep them (NASA NPR 7123 / ISO 15288 practice). Click a card to open its fillable form in the stage below; fields are greyed placeholders to fill and values autosave in this browser. Use “Open document · print/PDF” inside the open form, or “Open entire suite as printable HTML” above for all seven at once.</p>${docCardsHTML()}<div class="art-stage" id="docStage"></div></div>
`};
